frame.asks_ops:
Shane, you propose the engine orders, and your two vetoes bind on me. Please give me the following.

(1) PROPOSAL
Your orders for `gtf2_solo` (hold is its only legal value) and `jv_with_rr`, with the reasoning.

(2) READINESS
Set GTF2's 2036 ready year against every possible new EIS:
- an Embraer narrowbody launched in 2045: EIS 2049, on P&W engines. Now that GTF2 has eight years on NGSA, do you recommend GTF2 or the GTF family at the Advantage standard? It is Embraer's choice;
- an fps launched in 2045: 2052 on the 7-year ramp, 2055 on the 10-year ramp or via Embraer;
- the Joint Venture if formed now with GTF2 folded in: what ready date, and what would it bring that GTF2 does not?

(3) THE FLEET RECORD IS NOW THE DURABILITY TEST
Give me the GTF2 record on NGSA since 2037:
- time on wing;
- unscheduled removals;
- life-limited parts against full life;
- the severe-environment fleet;
- the GTF Hot Section kit's measured time on wing;
- the status of the CMC hot-section block deferred in 2035: proven, instrumented, or still waiting.
If the record is not in your evidence or the brief, say so plainly. I want the data, not reassurance. That decides whether the statement cites any figure.

(4) CASTINGS, FORGINGS AND SHOPS TO THE PEAK AND PAST IT
One plan for all these loads together:
- the NGSA ramp on the hold row: 1,299 engines (2045) to 1,449 (2049), 1,548 (2051) and the 1,597 peak (2052), then down 40% to 951 by 2060;
- a possible Embraer line (S3: EIS 2049, up to 8 aircraft a month six years after EIS, about 192 engines a year);
- a possible fps (S2: EIS 2055);
- MRO for the installed GTF and GTF2 fleet.
Forging takes 2 to 2.5 years to add [P-0079]. Tell me which tranches must be ordered by about 2049 for the 2051-52 step. Favour supplier and partner capacity over fixed plant the decline would strand. Balance the ramp jointly with Airbus [PX-0099, PX-0110], and the fleet keeps first call on material.

(5) ENGINEERING LOAD
Size the load together: GTF2 later blocks (CMC), Hot Section embodiment, a possible Embraer installation, a possible fps installation, and technology-only next-generation geared work inside the envelope. Can we carry all of it without taking people off the fleet?

(6) JOINT VENTURE, TECHNICAL
Does formation now put GTF2's gear and core into a shared programme? Do you raise the gear flag? Which terms would ever keep them out [P-1233]?

(7) VETO CHECKS
- Your two checks (durability proven before entry into service; parts and capacity) on Row A and Row B.
- Clear the draft statement for any durability claim the fleet has not shown.
- Say where your view rests on the seat's doctrine rather than your record. Your record is one event, June 2023.

